<title>UK: Abbey National ups two-year bond to $300 mln.</title>
<headline>Abbey National ups two-year bond to $300 mln.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond has been increased to $300 million from $200 million, lead manager Nikko said.</p>
<p> BORROWER   ABBEY NATIONAL TREASURY SERVICES</p>
<p> GUARANTOR  ABBEY NATIONAL PLC  (RATED AA2/AA)</p>
<p> AMT  **$300 MLN	COUPON     6.00	MATURITY    10.MAR.99</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE **99.97    PAY DATE    10.MAR.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  12.5 BP   REOFFER    99.97     SPREAD	+8 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	=	   LISTING    LONDON    PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  =	   DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS US/UK</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    2.5 BP    SELL CONC  10 BP     PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p> UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 5.875 PCT JANUARY 1999 U.S TREASURIES</p>
<p> NOTES	**ORIGINALLY LAUNCHED 10.FEB FOR $200 MLN AT 99.95</p>
<p>		UNSECURED AND UNSUBORDINATED</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
